WEEK 16 — MULTI-CASHIER DRAWERS AND HANDOVER

Date: Monday, 23 November 2026

Problem: With several cashiers, nobody could see the cash other desks held, and a new shift started with no float.

Solution:
- Each cashier has their own drawer, and the desk lists every drawer open today.
- The floor total is calculated on the server from all open drawers.
- A new cashier can take over the counted float of the colleague who closed last.
- A refund reduces the drawer it was paid from, so all totals stay consistent.
- Tests cover handover, floor totals, and refusing a refund bigger than the drawer.
